 crew, and steal the Golden Sardine.","/examples/moonlight-mayhem-codex/",{"_25":563,"_27":3943,"_29":3944,"_1160":1578,"_3377":3998,"_1157":145,"_133":1454,"_1152":3996,"_1145":3999,"_87":4000,"_80":4001,"_38":4002,"_1424":4003,"_1110":4004},[3948,3949,3950,3951,3952,3953,3954,3955,3956,3957,3958,3959,3960,3961,3962,3963,3964,3965,3966,3967],{"_59":27,"_72":3943,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":3944,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":1578,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":3375,"_99":100,"_65":3997,"_61":3377,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":104,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":1452,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":3996,"_61":1152,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":1142,"_99":1143,"_65":3991,"_61":1145,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1137,"_65":3987,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1441,"_72":1736,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1135,"_72":1136,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1129,"_65":3983,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":74,"_72":1128,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":122,"_65":3979,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1428,"_72":1429,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1422,"_65":3974,"_61":1424,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1108,"_65":3970,"_61":1110,"_77":-7},{"_59":97,"_61":1411,"_63":1412,"_65":3969},{"_59":1406,"_61":1407,"_63":625,"_581":3968,"_583":624,"_38":626,"_591":592,"_593":594,"_1409":1491},{"_59":69,"_61":1404,"_63":1405,"_72":590},"/GameMap/media/learning/moonlight-mayhem-codex.webp",[2169],[3971,3972,3973],{"_63":1258,"_31":1259},{"_63":1418,"_31":1419},{"_63":1197,"_31":1198},[3975],{"_63":3976,"_31":3977,"_85":3978},"Read the published Codex transcript","https://github.com/simonw/raccoon-heist-codex/blob/main/transcript.md","The creator links this development record from the build account; it accompanies the game source rather than a generator-only repository.",[3980],{"_63":1980,"_31":3981,"_85":3982},"https://github.com/simonw/raccoon-heist-codex/","Actual game source, committed textures, vendored Three.js, build notes, and transcript. No build step is required; use a local static HTTP server to run the repository.",[3984],{"_63":3985,"_31":626,"_85":3986},"Play Moonlight & Mayhem","Desktop: WASD or arrows to move, E to interact, Space or Shift to dash, Escape to pause. Mobile uses a touch stick and action buttons. Requires a WebGL-capable browser.",[3988],{"_63":3989,"_31":3990,"_85":-7},"Read the creator’s build and fix log","https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/7/moonlight-mayhem/",[3992,3993,3994,3995],"Play the heist and trace crew rescue, security detection, interactions, and escape.","Read the creator’s build account and compare the original brief with the result.","Follow the transcript and commit history to study scene construction, generated art, and the visual bug fix.","Serve the complete repository locally, then study one mechanic and its supporting assets.","Simon Willison documents giving Codex the game brief and image-generation access, then requesting a visual bug fix. The published project includes the game, generated textures, and the development transcript.",[3743],[3743],[3992,3993,3994,3995],{"_63":3989,"_31":3990,"_23":1755},{"_63":3985,"_31":626,"_23":1128,"_85":3986},{"_63":1980,"_31":3981,"_1463":1464,"_85":3982},{"_63":3976,"_31":3977,"_85":3978},[1289,1462,1231],"example:dinosaur-offline-gemini-cli","Dinosaur Game Offline: Gemini CLI-assisted runner","Jump a pixel dinosaur over cacti and avoid flying obstacles while the score and speed increase. This small browser game includes its complete JavaScript implementation, sprites, and sound effects.","/examples/dinosaur-offline-gemini-cli/",{"_25":485,"_27":4006,"_29":4007,"_1160":4060,"_1157":144,"_133":1454,"_1152":4059,"_1145":4061,"_87":4062,"_80":4063,"_38":4064,"_1424":4065,"_1110":4066},[4011,4012,4013,4014,4015,4016,4017,4018,4019,4020,4021,4022,4023,4024,4025,4026,4027,4028,4029],{"_59":27,"_72":4006,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":4007,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":4060,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":103,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":1452,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":4059,"_61":1152,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":1142,"_99":1143,"_65":4053,"_61":1145,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1137,"_65":4050,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1441,"_72":1442,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1135,"_72":1136,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1129,"_65":4046,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":74,"_72":1128,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":122,"_65":4041,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1428,"_72":1429,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1422,"_65":4036,"_61":1424,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1108,"_65":4033,"_61":1110,"_77":-7},{"_59":97,"_61":1411,"_63":1412,"_65":4031},{"_59":1406,"_61":1407,"_63":806,"_581":4030,"_583":805,"_38":807,"_591":592,"_593":594,"_1409":1491},{"_59":69,"_61":1404,"_63":1405,"_72":808},"/GameMap/media/learning/dinosaur-offline-gemini-cli.webp",[4032],"Gemini CLI",[4034],{"_63":4032,"_31":4035},"/resources/gemini-cli/",[4037],{"_63":4038,"_31":4039,"_85":4040},"See the creator’s Gemini CLI disclosure","https://github.com/tonidevvn/dinosaur-game-offline#how-gemini-cli-helped","README, repository description, and the in-game footer explicitly name gemini-cli. This establishes creator attribution rather than independent proof of fully autonomous generation.",[4042],{"_63":4043,"_31":4044,"_85":4045},"Open the complete dinosaur game source","https://github.com/tonidevvn/dinosaur-game-offline","Complete index.html, style.css, script.js, and referenced image/audio assets. Public source is available, but the repository does not declare a code license.",[4047],{"_63":4048,"_31":807,"_85":4049},"Play Dinosaur Game Offline","Author-hosted browser build; earlier catalog notes report a Chromium check, not independently revalidated here. Space starts and jumps; after a collision, click the restart icon. Desktop keyboard recommended because the board has a fixed 900-pixel width. The full project can also run locally by opening index.html.",[4051],{"_63":4052,"_31":4039,"_85":-7},"Read how Gemini CLI helped",[4054,4055,4056,4057,4058],"Open the author-hosted browser game on a desktop with a keyboard. Press Space once to start, then press Space again to jump over an approaching cactus.","Watch the score rise, test a collision, and use the restart icon after game over. Earlier catalog notes report a start/jump/score/collision/restart smoke test and a preview captured during a jump. That run was not repeated or independently validated in this source-only review.","To run locally, download the complete dinosaur-game-offline repository and open index.html. Keep style.css, script.js, and public/ beside it. No npm installation, build step, Gemini CLI, or API key is needed to play.","If a browser restricts local files, serve the repository with python3 -m http.server 8080 and open http://localhost:8080. The game board is fixed at 900 pixels wide and targets desktop keyboard play. Its optional Google Fonts stylesheet uses the network.","Read the creator’s disclosure, then inspect script.js for the requestAnimationFrame loop, jump state, obstacle spawning, scoring, collision checks, and restart behavior.","The creator explicitly credits Gemini CLI with scaffolding, game logic, debugging, and improvements in the README and game footer. No original conversation or exact model identifier is published; this is a documented assisted build.","DOM / CSS · JavaScript",[4054,4055,4056,4057,4058],{"_63":4052,"_31":4039,"_23":1442},{"_63":4048,"_31":807,"_23":1128,"_85":4049},{"_63":4043,"_31":4044,"_85":4045,"_1463":1464},{"_63":4038,"_31":4039,"_85":4040},[4067],"gemini-cli","example:cloud-crush-gemini-cli","Cloud Crush: Gemini CLI builds a match-3 game","Match cloud-service icons on an eight-by-eight board, chase a timed high score, and create special Gemini gems. Google publishes the complete Go game alongside a detailed Gemini CLI codelab.","/examples/cloud-crush-gemini-cli/",{"_25":483,"_27":4069,"_29":4070,"_1160":4127,"_1157":144,"_133":1454,"_1152":4126,"_1145":4128,"_87":4129,"_80":4130,"_38":4131,"_1424":4132,"_1110":4133},[4074,4075,4076,4077,4078,4079,4080,4081,4082,4083,4084,4085,4086,4087,4088,4089,4090,4091,4092,4093],{"_59":27,"_72":4069,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":4070,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":4127,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":103,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":1452,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":4126,"_61":1152,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":1142,"_99":1143,"_65":4119,"_61":1145,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1137,"_65":4115,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1441,"_72":87,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1135,"_72":2052,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1129,"_65":4110,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":74,"_72":1434,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":122,"_65":4105,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1428,"_72":1429,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1422,"_65":4100,"_61":1424,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1108,"_65":4098,"_61":1110,"_77":-7},{"_59":97,"_61":1411,"_63":1412,"_65":4097},{"_59":1406,"_61":1407,"_63":811,"_581":4096,"_583":810,"_38":812,"_591":592,"_593":594,"_1409":1899},{"_59":69,"_61":1896,"_63":1897,"_72":590},{"_59":60,"_61":1892,"_63":1893,"_65":4094},[4095],{"_63":1893,"_31":813},"/GameMap/media/learning/cloud-crush-gemini-cli.webp",[4032],[4099],{"_63":4032,"_31":4035},[4101],{"_63":4102,"_31":4103,"_85":4104},"See Google’s explicit Gemini CLI attribution","https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/devrel-demos/blob/main/codelabs/gemini-cli/gemini-cli-match3-golang/README.md","The publisher README explicitly names Gemini CLI; the separate official codelab records the development prompts and human steering workflow.",[4106],{"_63":4107,"_31":4108,"_85":4109},"Open the complete Go game project","https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/devrel-demos/tree/main/codelabs/gemini-cli/gemini-cli-match3-golang","Includes main.go, source images and audio, go.mod, browser entry and runtime helper, server/main.go, Dockerfile, and publisher screenshots. The repository code is Apache-2.0. A WASM binary must be built locally.",[4111],{"_63":4112,"_31":4113,"_85":4114},"Download & run Cloud Crush","https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/devrel-demos/blob/main/codelabs/gemini-cli/gemini-cli-match3-golang/README.md#local-development","Local Go / WASM project; no hosted public game endpoint was verified. Use Go 1.26.2+ and run go run . from the game directory. Expand the steps for the complete browser build, asset copy, matching wasm_exec.js, and local server commands. Native play needs a graphical desktop and working audio drivers. Cloud Crush was not compiled locally in this review.",[4116],{"_63":4117,"_31":4118,"_85":-7},"Follow Google’s Gemini CLI game codelab","https://codelabs.developers.google.com/next26/gemini-cli-match3-golang",[4120,4121,4122,4123,4124,4125],"Download the devrel-demos repository and enter codelabs/gemini-cli/gemini-cli-match3-golang. Install Go 1.26.2 or newer; the README’s 1.24+ prerequisite is outdated. For native desktop play, run: go run .","Follow the title and player-name prompts. Use arrow keys to move the cursor and Space to select a gem, then an arrow to swap. Mouse/touch input is also implemented. Compare matching, falling tiles, time bonuses, and score behavior with main.go.","For a local browser build, first prepare the files served by the Go server: mkdir -p public/assets; cp assets/* public/assets/; cp index.html public/index.html. The committed public/assets directory is missing source files required by the game, including background.jpg.","Use the WASM helper from the same Go installation as the compiler: cp \"$(go env GOROOT)/lib/wasm/wasm_exec.js\" public/wasm_exec.js. Then compile: GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build -o public/cloud-crush.wasm .","Run the browser server from the same game directory: go run server/main.go. Open http://localhost:8080. Local play does not require Gemini CLI, an API key, a Google Cloud account, or cloud deployment.","Read the official codelab to trace the development prompts. The browser instructions above were checked against source; this review did not install Go or compile the game. Its preview is a publisher-provided gameplay screenshot.","Google’s repository attributes game generation to Gemini CLI. The official codelab shows human orchestration through plan mode, steering prompts, browser adaptation, testing, and subagents. That is publisher evidence, not an independent measurement of autonomous authorship.","Ebitengine 2 · Go / WebAssembly",[4120,4121,4122,4123,4124,4125],{"_63":4117,"_31":4118,"_23":87},{"_63":4112,"_31":4113,"_23":1434,"_85":4114},{"_63":4107,"_31":4108,"_85":4109,"_1463":1464},{"_63":4102,"_31":4103,"_85":4104},[4067],"example:roo-code-action","Action with AI: a Roo Code experiment","A small SVG top-down action prototype with mouse-aimed shooting, enemies and telegraphed attacks, paired with a detailed account of prompt-driven implementation.","/examples/roo-code-action/",{"_25":481,"_27":4135,"_29":4136,"_1160":4184,"_1157":144,"_1152":4183,"_1145":4185,"_87":4186,"_80":4187,"_38":4188,"_1424":4189,"_133":1454,"_1110":4190},[4140,4141,4142,4143,4144,4145,4146,4147,4148,4149,4150,4151,4152,4153,4154,4155,4156,4157],{"_59":27,"_72":4135,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":4136,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":4184,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":103,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":1452,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":4183,"_61":1152,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":1142,"_99":1143,"_65":4178,"_61":1145,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1137,"_65":4175,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1441,"_72":1736,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1135,"_72":1136,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1129,"_65":4171,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":74,"_72":1128,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":122,"_65":4166,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1428,"_72":1429,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1422,"_65":4161,"_61":1424,"_77":-7},{"_59":97,"_61":1411,"_63":1412,"_65":4159},{"_59":1406,"_61":1407,"_63":816,"_581":4158,"_583":815,"_38":817,"_591":592,"_593":594,"_1409":1491},{"_59":69,"_61":1404,"_63":1405,"_72":94},"/GameMap/media/learning/roo-code-action.webp",[4160],"Roo Code",[4162],{"_63":4163,"_31":4164,"_85":4165},"Read the original AI development account","https://zenn.dev/mizchi/articles/game-with-cline","The author names Roo Code and Claude 3.5 Sonnet, explains the no-direct-coding constraint and documents the human design and steering role.",[4167],{"_63":4168,"_31":4169,"_85":4170},"Open the complete action prototype","https://github.com/mizchi/action-with-ai","Complete React/TypeScript project with SVG rendering, movement, collision, combat, shared types, tests and development notes. No repository license file was found in the reviewed tree.",[4172],{"_63":4173,"_31":817,"_85":4174},"Play Action with AI","Early desktop keyboard-and-mouse prototype. WASD moves and holding the mouse button fires; visual polish and a full commercial campaign are outside its scope.",[4176],{"_63":4177,"_31":4164,"_85":-7},"Read the creator’s Roo Code experiment",[4179,4180,4181,4182],"Move with WASD, aim with the mouse and hold the mouse button to shoot.","Read the original sequence from rendering and movement through enemy health and attack warnings.","Inspect docs/overview.md, the shared types and combat modules alongside the creator’s discussion of documentation drift.","For local study, install the project dependencies with the documented pnpm setup and run pnpm dev, then change one attack or movement rule.","Mizchi explicitly used Roo Code, formerly Roo Cline, with Claude 3.5 Sonnet while forbidding direct human code edits. The human supplied an experienced developer’s design, incremental instructions and architecture constraints. The published article includes the workflow and limitations; this is an early prototype.","React · SVG · TypeScript",[4179,4180,4181,4182],{"_63":4177,"_31":4164,"_23":1755},{"_63":4173,"_31":817,"_23":1128,"_85":4174},{"_63":4168,"_31":4169,"_85":4170,"_1463":1464},{"_63":4163,"_31":4164,"_85":4165},[],"example:three-quake-claude-port","Three Quake: an AI-assisted Quake port","Play Quake’s shareware episode in a Three.js browser port, and study how an existing shooter’s rendering and runtime were adapted with AI assistance.","/examples/three-quake-claude-port/",{"_25":479,"_27":4192,"_29":4193,"_1160":1578,"_1157":145,"_1152":4243,"_1145":4244,"_87":4245,"_80":4246,"_38":4247,"_1424":4248,"_1110":4249,"_133":1454},[4197,4198,4199,4200,4201,4202,4203,4204,4205,4206,4207,4208,4209,4210,4211,4212,4213,4214,4215],{"_59":27,"_72":4192,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":4193,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":1578,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":104,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":1452,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":4243,"_61":1152,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":1142,"_99":1143,"_65":4238,"_61":1145,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1137,"_65":4234,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1441,"_72":1442,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1135,"_72":1136,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1129,"_65":4230,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":74,"_72":1128,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":122,"_65":4225,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1428,"_72":1429,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1422,"_65":4220,"_61":1424,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1108,"_65":4218,"_61":1110,"_77":-7},{"_59":97,"_61":1411,"_63":1412,"_65":4217},{"_59":1406,"_61":1407,"_63":820,"_581":4216,"_583":819,"_38":821,"_591":592,"_593":594,"_1409":1491},{"_59":69,"_61":1404,"_63":1405,"_72":94},"/GameMap/media/learning/three-quake-claude-port.webp",[1552],[4219],{"_63":1418,"_31":1419},[4221],{"_63":4222,"_31":4223,"_85":4224},"Read the author’s AI and original-game credits","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake#credits","The maintainer distinguishes id Software’s original game from the Three.js port made with Claude assistance.",[4226],{"_63":4227,"_31":4228,"_85":4229},"Open the complete browser port","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake","Complete browser port, maps, runtime source and tests, with the shareware pak0.pak. Code is GPL-2.0; original Quake game data has separate terms and is not relicensed by the code license.",[4231],{"_63":4232,"_31":821,"_85":4233},"Play Three Quake","Keyboard, mouse and a WebGL-capable browser. The included shareware data covers Episode 1; full-game content is separate.",[4235],{"_63":4236,"_31":4237,"_85":-7},"Read the port credits and creator dev log","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake#dev-log",[4239,4240,4241,4242],"Open the browser build, start a new single-player game and test the movement and firing controls.","Read the creator’s port credits and dev log alongside the original id Software source reference.","Inspect the browser renderer, game runtime, maps and tests to trace how the existing game was adapted.","Use the included shareware data for Episode 1; a registered full-game data set is separate and must be supplied by its owner.","Mr.doob credits Claude for assistance with the Three.js port. Quake’s game design and original implementation belong to id Software; this is an AI-assisted port, not a claim that AI created Quake. The README links a creator dev log without identifying a particular Claude client.",[4239,4240,4241,4242],{"_63":4236,"_31":4237,"_23":1442},{"_63":4232,"_31":821,"_23":1128,"_85":4233},{"_63":4227,"_31":4228,"_85":4229,"_1463":1464},{"_63":4222,"_31":4223,"_85":4224},[1462],"example:crown-defender-codex","Crown Defender TD 3D · Codex build","Control a hero under an isometric camera, defend a castle through thirty waves and choose upgrades to unlock a cosmetic crown.","/examples/crown-defender-codex/",{"_25":477,"_27":4251,"_29":4252,"_1160":1578,"_1157":145,"_133":2260,"_1152":4302,"_1145":4303,"_87"