https://github.com/Aleksandr-Litvinenko/Codex.-Crown-Defender-TD-3D-browser-tower-defense-game/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","Static browser game. Run python3 -m http.server 8010 and open localhost:8010/index.html; choose Играть (Play). Russian interface. WASD/arrows move; semicolon attacks. Mobile joystick/buttons included. Optional two-player mode requires node server/multiplayer-server.mjs.",[4295],{"_63":4296,"_31":4283,"_85":-7},"Read the same-brief agent comparison",[4298,4299,4300,4301],"Serve the project locally and enter TD Defense.","Read the original requirements and same-brief comparison.","Inspect hero movement, wave progression and upgrade logic.","Change one upgrade and test losing, retrying and saved progress.","Aleksandr-Litvinenko attributes this build to Codex and publishes a comparison with a Claude Code version made from the same brief. The author states that the comparison concerns the agents’ original implementation choices, with assets and runtime code included here.",[4298,4299,4300,4301],{"_63":4296,"_31":4283,"_23":1755},{"_63":4291,"_31":4292,"_23":1434,"_85":4293},{"_63":4287,"_31":825,"_1463":1464,"_85":4288},{"_63":4282,"_31":4283,"_85":4284},[1289,1462],"example:arkanoid-neon-claude","Arkanoid Neon","Bounce the ball through eight neon brick layouts, collect power-ups and keep the rally alive as the stages accelerate. This complete browser game uses Canvas 2D and synthesized Web Audio.","/examples/arkanoid-neon-claude/",{"_25":475,"_27":4310,"_29":4311,"_1160":4364,"_1157":144,"_133":2260,"_1152":4363,"_1145":4365,"_87":4366,"_80":4367,"_38":4368,"_1424":4369,"_1110":4370},[4315,4316,4317,4318,4319,4320,4321,4322,4323,4324,4325,4326,4327,4328,4329,4330,4331,4332,4333,4334],{"_59":27,"_72":4310,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":4311,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":4364,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":103,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":2259,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":