 to track selection. Source-checked launch steps; not executed.",[5218],{"_63":5219,"_31":5205,"_85":-7},"Read the tool and model disclosure",[5221,5222,5223,5224],"Download the source and launch the Pygame window with Python 3.12 or newer.","Race a supplied track and compare the player ghost with the unlockable creator ghost.","Read the development disclosure, then inspect movement, lap timing, and replay storage.","Change a track or handling parameter and complete a validation run before saving.","Kecksdose names OpenCode as the coding tool and GPT 5.2 Codex as the model. The README publishes a short development disclosure, rather than the original prompts or full conversation.","Pygame 2.6 · Python",[5221,5222,5223,5224],{"_63":5219,"_31":5205,"_23":1442},{"_63":5214,"_31":5215,"_23":1434,"_85":5216},{"_63":5209,"_31":5210,"_1463":1464,"_85":5211},{"_63":5204,"_31":5205,"_85":5206},[5233],"opencode","example:golden-hour-skatepark-cursor","Golden Hour Skatepark","Skate an original beachside park: carve transitions, ollie, flip, grind, manual, bail and recover. This complete third-person sandbox has transient trick combos and a changeable time of day, with no levels or persistent score.","/examples/golden-hour-skatepark-cursor/",{"_25":445,"_27":5235,"_29":5236,"_1160":5294,"_3377":5295,"_1157":145,"_133":1454,"_1152":5292,"_1145":5296,"_87":5297,"_80":5298,"_38":5299,"_1424":5300,"_1110":5301},[5240,5241,5242,5243,5244,5245,5246,5247,5248,5249,5250,5251,5252,5253,5254,5255,5256,5257,5258,5259,5260],{"_59":27,"_72":5235,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":5236,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":5294,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":3375,"_99":100,"_65":5293,"_61":3377,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":104,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":1452,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":5292,"_61":1152,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":1142,"_99":1143,"_65":5287,"_61":1145,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1137,"_65":5283,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1441,"_72":1736,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1135,"_72":1136,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1129,"_65":5278,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":74,"_72":1128,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":122,"_65":5273,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1428,"_72":1429,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1422,"_65":5268,"_61":1424,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1108,"_65":5265,"_61":1110,"_77":-7},{"_59":97,"_61":1411,"_63":1412,"_65":5264},{"_59":1406,"_61":1407,"_63":903,"_581":5263,"_583":902,"_38":904,"_591":592,"_593":594,"_1409":1899},{"_59":69,"_61":1896,"_63":1897,"_72":94},{"_59":60,"_61":1892,"_63":1893,"_65":5261},[5262],{"_63":1893,"_31":905},"/GameMap/media/learning/golden-hour-skatepark-cursor.webp",[1782],[5266,5267],{"_63":1418,"_31":1419},{"_63":1115,"_31":1116},[5269],{"_63":5270,"_31":5271,"_85":5272},"Read the creator’s Cursor contribution account","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park#how-it-was-built","The README explicitly names Cursor AI agents and separates builder passes, critic feedback and human playtests; docs/MAKING-OF.md provides a detailed account. Source-checked; performance and playability claims were not reproduced.",[5274],{"_63":5275,"_31":5276,"_85":5277},"Open the complete skating project","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park","Complete TypeScript game, procedural park code, runtime skater/crowd GLBs, textures, audio and source tools. CI uses Node 22 and pnpm 10.18.0; pnpm install then pnpm dev at 127.0.0.1:5188. Ports are fixed. No root LICENSE was found; CC0 media, Mixamo animations and dependencies keep separate terms.",[5279],{"_63":5280,"_31":5281,"_85":5282},"Play Golden Hour Skatepark","https://starknightt.github.io/skate-park/","Browser skating sandbox with keyboard, optional mouse/gamepad and touch controls. Press any key, click or tap to take over from the title-screen rider. Phone testing reported by the creator used desktop emulation; Firefox and desktop Safari remain untested.",[5284],{"_63":5285,"_31":5286,"_85":-7},"Read the builder-and-critic development account","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park/blob/main/docs/MAKING-OF.md",[5288,5289,5290,5291],"Play the park and test pushing, carving, one trick, a bail and recovery.","Read the making-of account and separate human feedback, agent implementation and third-party assets.","Use Node 22 with pnpm 10.18.0, then pnpm install and pnpm dev; inspect the collision mesh and character pipeline.","Ask an agent to adjust one movement or camera parameter, then compare transition riding, tricks and recovery across the park.","The author says Cursor AI agents implemented the game through builder and visual-critic passes, with human playtests refining controls. Code-built environments and procedural riding are combined with Cursor-generated artwork, credited CC0 audio/textures and Mixamo recovery animations.",[1115],"Three.js · TypeScript",[1115],[5288,5289,5290,5291],{"_63":5285,"_31":5286,"_23":1755},{"_63":5280,"_31":5281,"_23":1128,"_85":5282},{"_63":5275,"_31":5276,"_1463":1464,"_85":5277},{"_63":5270,"_31":5271,"_85":5272},[1462,1169],"example:castle-clash-duel-claude","Castle Clash Duel","Recruit warriors and archers and fight a two-player tactical battle on a tilemap. This complete Phaser prototype pairs Claude Code implementation with Pixel Frog’s Tiny Swords artwork.","/examples/castle-clash-duel-claude/",{"_25":443,"_27":5303,"_29":5304,"_1160":2674,"_1157":144,"_133":1454,"_1152":5355,"_1145":5356,"_87":5357,"_80":5358,"_38":5359,"_1424":5360,"_1110":5361},[5308,5309,5310,5311,5312,5313,5314,5315,5316,5317,5318,5319,5320,5321,5322,5323,5324,5325,5326,5327],{"_59":27,"_72":5303,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":5304,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":2674,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":103,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":1452,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":5355,"_61":1152,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":1142,"_99":1143,"_65":5350,"_61":1145,"_