e","MIT-licensed Assets, Packages, ProjectSettings, scenes, and C# gameplay source. Requires Unity 6000.4.11f1; open Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity and press Play. Windows/WebGL build modules are needed only for packaging; Claude/MCP tooling is not required for play.",[5465],{"_63":5466,"_31":5467,"_85":5468},"Download morBreaker for Windows or WebGL","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker/releases/tag/v1.2.0","Version 1.2.0 includes Windows standalone and WebGL ZIPs. Extract the Windows build and launch it, or serve the WebGL build over HTTP. A/D or arrows move, Space launches, H shows scores, and Space/Enter restarts. Pointer/touch controls are included; no public hosted play link is supplied.",[5470],{"_63":5471,"_31":5458,"_85":-7},"Read the creator’s Unity and Claude Code account",[5473,5474,5475,5476],"Download the Windows release or serve the published WebGL build over HTTP.","Try paddle steering, acceleration, loss, restart, and the local score list.","Read the creator’s Claude Code disclosure and inspect the gameplay C# scripts.","Open SampleScene.unity with Unity 6000.4.11f1, change one level rule, and test progression.","KingMordas says Claude Code built almost the entire game through the Unity MCP plugin: gameplay scripts, scene and prefab wiring, tests, and documentation. The AI editor tooling is separate from the released game runtime.","Unity 6 · URP · C#",[5473,5474,5475,5476],{"_63":5471,"_31":5458,"_23":1442},{"_63":5466,"_31":5467,"_23":1434,"_85":5468},{"_63":5462,"_31":919,"_1463":1464,"_85":5463},{"_63":5457,"_31":5458,"_85":5459},[4434,1754],"example:deep-yellow-claude","DEEP YELLOW","Explore procedural Backrooms in a first-person, turn-based roguelike. Moving or waiting triggers combat, while equipment combinations and sanity shape each run.","/examples/deep-yellow-claude/",{"_25":437,"_27":5486,"_29":5487,"_1160":2131,"_1157":145,"_133":1454,"_1152":5544,"_1145":5545,"_87":5546,"_80":5547,"_38":5548,"_1424":5549,"_1110":5550,"_2113":5551},[5491,5492,5493,5494,5495,5496,5497,5498,5499,5500,5501,5502,5503,5504,5505,5506,5507,5508,5509,5510,5511],{"_59":27,"_72":5486,"_61":27,"_77":-7},{"_59":134,"_72":5487,"_61":29,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1158,"_72":2131,"_61":1160,"_77":128},{"_59":69,"_63":1156,"_72":104,"_61":1157,"_77":96},{"_59":69,"_63":1153,"_72":1452,"_61":133,"_77":1155},{"_59":69,"_63":1150,"_72":5544,"_61":1152,"_77":128},{"_59":97,"_63":1142,"_99":1143,"_65":5539,"_61":1145,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1137,"_65":5536,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1441,"_72":1736,"_61":87,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1135,"_72":283,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1129,"_65":5532,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":74,"_72":1128,"_61":80,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":2111,"_65":5528,"_61":2113,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":122,"_65":5524,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":69,"_63":1428,"_72":1429,"_61":38,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1422,"_65":5519,"_61":1424,"_77":-7},{"_59":60,"_63":1108,"_65":5516,"_61":1110,"_77":-7},{"_59":97,"_61":1411,"_63":1412,"_65":5515},{"_59":1406,"_61":1407,"_63":922,"_581":5514,"_583":921,"_38":923,"_591":592,"_593":594,"_1409":1899},{"_59":69,"_61":1896,"_63":1897,"_72":94},{"_59":60,"_61":1892,"_63":1893,"_65":5512},[5513],{"_63":1893,"_31":924},"/GameMap/media/learning/deep-yellow-claude.webp",[1717],[5517,5518],{"_63":1121,"_31":1122},{"_63":1717,"_31":1721},[5520],{"_63":5521,"_31":5522,"_85":5523},"Read the explicit Claude Code credit","https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/blob/master/CREDITS.md#code-and-design","Creator attribution specifically names Claude via Claude Code. The itch page separately discloses AI assistance for code; no complete session transcript is supplied.",[5525],{"_63":2044,"_31":5526,"_85":5527},"https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow","Full Godot 4.6 project, scenes, scripts, assets, shaders, and export presets. The itch page lists code MIT and assets CC0, while CREDITS.md still leaves the original-code license undecided and some third-party licenses unspecified; inspect both before reuse.",[5529],{"_63":1922,"_31":5530,"_85":5531},"https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/releases/tag/v0.13.0","Download — Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.",[5533],{"_63":5534,"_31":923,"_85":5535},"Play DEEP YELLOW","In-development browser build plus Windows/Linux downloads. The creator recommends Chrome or a controller; Firefox mouse input has known problems. Includes horror themes and an interactive tutorial.",[5537],{"_63":5538,"_31":923,"_85":-7},"Read the creator’s game and development notes",[5540,5541,5542,5543],"Play the interactive tutorial and compare moving, waiting, equipment, and sanity.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the project’s separate attribution file.","Import project.godot in Godot 4.6 and inspect the start menu, procedural levels, and turn systems.","Change one equipment or turn rule, then test a complete run and restart.","Drew Brereton identifies the game as code-assisted by Claude. The project credits specifically name Claude Code and distinguish original work from external shaders, textures, and fonts.",[5540,5541,5542,5543],{"_63":5538,"_31":923,"_23":1755},{"_63":5534,"_31":923,"_23":1128,"_85":5535},{"_63":2044,"_31":5526,"_1463":1464,"_85":5527},{"_63":5521,"_31":5522,"_85":5523},[1166,1754],[5552],{"_2140":1922,"_31":5530,"_23":1434,"_85":5553},"Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.","example:surge-for-oinja-codex","SURGE for Oinja","Shape an electrical build while surviving mechanical swarms across two interactive maps. Automatic attacks leave movement, dodging, upgrades and facility restoration to the player.","/examples/surge-for-oinja-codex/",{"_25":435,"_27":5555,"_29":5